{#
    The bar under a purchase document's line table: a [charge type] select plus an Add Line
    control — the buy-side twin of sales_add_line_bar.html.twig. Include it rather than copying it.

    It does not add PRODUCT rows. It adds a CHARGE row — freight, tax or a one-off fee — which the
    document posts back as charge_lines[] and PurchaseDocumentChargeLines turns into that
    document's freight lines, manual tax lines and manual fee lines. It is the only way to set
    freight at all, the same way the sell side's bar is the only way to set shipping.

    Shared by purchase_order_edit.html.twig and bill_edit.html.twig, which is the fix for
    VendorBillController's own charge model having drifted onto a completely different shape
    (`charges[]` plus a bolted-on manual-tax box) — see _purchase_charge_row.html.twig's own
    docblock. One definition cannot drift.

    No `shippingOptions` the sell side's bar takes: there is no live carrier-rate lookup on the
    buy side to offer a rate choice from, so every shipping/fee/tax row here is typed, same as
    PurchaseOrder's form already did before this rewrite. `categoryFilter` IS taken (#full-parity,
    2026-09-15, corrected — it was wrongly grouped with `shippingOptions` above as though both
    needed live rate data; the filter is pure client-side option-hiding over the static list below,
    the same as the sell side's, and PO's earlier lack of it was an omission, not a difference):
    a JS-only Shipping/Tax/Fee picker in front of the full select, same wording as the sell side's
    — no divergent buy-side label. The underlying charge type key stays `freight` (see
    PurchaseChargeLine::TYPE_FREIGHT and `chargeTypeCategory()` in app.js, which files it under
    the shared 'shipping' filter category) — that is a backend/data enum name, not user-visible
    text, and renaming it is a separate, larger change (touches persisted charge_line rows).

    `hook: 'po'` (#full-parity, 2026-09-15) adds the JS "Add Line" button app.js's
    addSellDocChargeRow('po') binds to, plus the class the select needs for it to read the chosen
    type — the same pair the sell side's own bar renders under `hook`. The submit stays exactly
    where it was: this document's whole "no <noscript> wrapper" convention was that the server-
    rendered controls simply ARE what shows, and that is still true for the submit here — a JS
    admin never sees it because `.no-js-inline` hides it once the JS button beside it works, same
    as the sell side's does. `hook: ''` (default, VendorBill's current state) renders exactly as
    before: no JS button, no hook classes, the submit is simply the control.

    Parameters
    ----------
    submitLabel     required  the text on the submit that adds a row server-side.
    hook            optional  'po' for the live JS "Add Line" button, '' (default) for the original
                              submit-only bar.
    sentinel        optional  defaults to false. Emits the charge_lines_present hidden input — see
                              the note below on why a create screen with nothing stored yet omits it.
    categoryFilter  optional  defaults to false. Adds the JS-only Freight/Tax/Fee category picker
                              in front of the full select — see the note above.

    ## charge_lines_present, and why a brand-new document does not carry it

    A document that is REBUILT from what its form posts cannot tell "the admin removed every
    charge row" from "this post was never shown the charge rows" — both arrive as no
    charge_lines[] — and guessing wrong wipes a stored document's freight, tax adjustments and
    manual fees on the first innocent save. So a form editing a STORED document renders this
    marker beside the control that shows the rows, and only a post carrying it is allowed to clear
    charges. PurchaseOrderController and VendorBillController both read it that way. A brand-new
    document has nothing stored to protect, so its create screen passes `sentinel: false`.
#}
{% set _hook = hook|default('') %}
<div class="purchase-charge-bar">
    {% if categoryFilter|default(false) and _hook %}
        <select class="js-{{ _hook }}-charge-category js-only" aria-label="Filter line type by category">
            <option value="">All types</option>
            <option value="shipping">Shipping</option>
            <option value="tax">Tax</option>
            <option value="fee">Fee</option>
        </select>
    {% endif %}
    <select{% if _hook %} class="js-{{ _hook }}-charge-type"{% endif %} name="charge_line_type" aria-label="Select line type to add">
        <option value=""></option>
        <option value="freight:Shipping">Shipping</option>
        <option value="fee:Brokerage">Brokerage</option>
        <option value="fee:Duty">Duty</option>
        <option value="fee:Fuel Surcharge">Fuel Surcharge</option>
        <option value="empty-freight:">Empty Freight Line (Type Anything)</option>
        <option value="empty-tax:">Empty Tax Line (Type Anything)</option>
        <option value="empty-fee:">Empty Fee Line (Type Anything)</option>
    </select>
    {% if _hook %}
        <select class="js-{{ _hook }}-charge-placement-choice js-only" aria-label="Fee placement" hidden>
            <option value="main_line">Main Line</option>
            <option value="before_tax_line">Before Tax</option>
            <option value="after_tax_line">After Tax</option>
        </select>
        <button class="button primary js-{{ _hook }}-bottom-add" type="button">Add Line</button>
    {% endif %}
    <button class="button primary{% if _hook %} no-js-inline{% endif %}" type="submit" name="add_charge_line" value="1">{{ submitLabel }}</button>
</div>
{% if sentinel|default(false) %}
    <input type="hidden" name="charge_lines_present" value="1">
{% endif %}
